---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Security & Privacy — CodeContext" description="Current CodeContext security, privacy, and transparency information.">
  <section class="hero container">
    <span class="kicker">TRUST / TRANSPARENCY</span>
    <h1>Know what CodeContext<br /><span>does with your data.</span></h1>
    <p>This page describes the current implementation. It is intentionally limited to behavior that exists today.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container grid">
    <article><span class="kicker">LOCAL-FIRST</span><h2>Repository analysis</h2><p>CodeContext analyzes repositories locally. With AI disabled, repository analysis and deterministic intelligence do not send repository content to a CodeContext telemetry or storage service.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">AI / OPT-IN</span><h2>Provider boundaries</h2><p>AI-assisted workflows are optional. When configured, bounded repository-derived context is sent directly to the selected provider for the requested AI operation. AI is not treated as the authoritative source of repository truth.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">REPORTS</span><h2>Self-contained output</h2><p>Generated HTML reports contain their visualization code and do not require a browser CDN request at report-open time. Reports can therefore be inspected offline.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">API BOUNDARY</span><h2>Trusted local use</h2><p>The local REST server validates repository paths and applies rate limiting, but it does not currently provide authentication, tenant isolation, or deployment-level authorization. Do not expose it publicly without an appropriate security boundary.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">CONTEXT LIMITS</span><h2>Bounded AI input</h2><p>AI operations use bounded repository-derived context rather than sending an entire repository indiscriminately. See the detailed privacy document for current implementation-level limits.</p></article>
    <article><span class="kicker">SOURCE</span><h2>Inspect the implementation</h2><p>CodeContext is open source. The exact implementation, configuration, and current behavior can be inspected directly in the repository.</p></article>
  </section>

  <section class="container links">
    <a href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/CodeContext/blob/main/docs/DATA_PRIVACY.md">Read the detailed transparency document ↗</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/CodeContext/blob/main/SECURITY.md">Read the security policy ↗</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/sonii-shivansh/CodeContext/issues">Report an issue ↗</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 110px 0 65px; max-width: 960px; }.kicker { color: var(--accent); font: 600 .72rem/1.2 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; }
  h1 { margin: 18px 0; font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem); line-height: .96; letter-spacing: -.065em; } h1 span { color: var(--muted); }.hero p { max-width: 700px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 12px; }.grid article { min-height: 210px; padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel); }.grid h2 { margin: 15px 0 8px; font-size: 1.3rem; }.grid p { color: var(--muted); }
  .links { margin-top: 70px; display: grid; gap: 8px; }.links a { padding: 18px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 9px; text-decoration: none; background: var(--panel); }.links a:hover { border-color: #304155; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
